{"errno":0,"errmsg":"","security":false,"data":{"id":"5980","title":"Xiaomi Vision Gran Turismo Makes Global Debut at MWC Barcelona 2026","desc":"Redefining the Future of Hypercar Design in the Electrification and AI Era","view_cnt":"27886","like_cnt":"15","add_time":"1772422094","haslike":false,"image_url":["https://i02.appmifile.com/512_operatorx_operatorx_opx/02/03/2026/6049d06bdadf0656804ecab80ae79e97.jpg"],"video_url":"","ad":{"title":"","link":"","image_url":""},"content":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eBarcelona, SPAIN, March 2, 2026\u003c/strong\u003e\u0026nbsp;— Following its unveiling at Xiaomi's global launch event, Xiaomi today revealed the full-scale concept model of Xiaomi Vision Gran Turismo at MWC 2026, a visionary electric hypercar concept created for the legendary\u0026nbsp;\u003cem\u003eGran Turismo\u003c/em\u003e\u0026nbsp;franchise. More than just a concept vehicle, it represents the first time a technology company has been invited to join the elite Vision Gran Turismo project, marking a historic milestone in both automotive design and virtual mobility.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe journey began last year at the GT World Series in London, where Kazunori Yamauchi, Producer of the\u0026nbsp;\u003cem\u003eGran Turismo \u003c/em\u003eseries, extended a personal invitation to Xiaomi. For any automotive designer, the opportunity to create a Vision Gran Turismo is a chance to set aside real-world constraints and imagine the ultimate driving experience from a clean sheet. For Xiaomi's global EV design team, it was an opportunity to approach hypercar design from a technology company's perspective, merging cutting-edge aerodynamics with AI-driven intelligence.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\"The invitation itself was a recognition of what Xiaomi has achieved,\" said Tianyuan Li, Design Head of Xiaomi Auto. \"It allowed our teams in Munich, Beijing, and Shanghai to collaborate, to push boundaries, and to envision what a future hypercar could look like when designed without limits.\"\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"//i02.appmifile.com/269_operatorx_operatorx_uploadTiptapImage/01/03/2026/bf8661c28aaa43d67135acb074a4d6b7.jpg\" alt=\"A silver sports car is parked on a smooth surface, with a streamlined body design featuring high-performance elements, and the background is an open gradient tone.\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2\u003eSculpted by the Wind: The Pursuit of Aerodynamic Balance\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eAt the heart of Xiaomi Vision Gran Turismo lies a fundamental question that every hypercar must answer: whether to prioritize extreme low drag for straight-line speed or maximum downforce to conquer corners. For an electric hypercar, Xiaomi believes neither extreme is the optimal solution. The true breakthrough lies in finding the perfect balance between the two, a pursuit of aerodynamic efficiency rather than singular metrics.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"//i02.appmifile.com/594_operatorx_operatorx_uploadTiptapImage/01/03/2026/4e9ab36ce77115dc024e8f10dbdb8a0d.png\" alt=\"A sleek car appears against a dark background, surrounded by effects resembling wind, with the text \u0026quot;SCULPTED BY THE WIND\u0026quot; positioned in the center.\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThis philosophy gave birth to the concept's core design principle: \"Sculpted by the Wind.\" Xiaomi Vision Gran Turismo is designed to meet aerodynamic needs without add-on attachments. This \"less is more\" mindset gives every element a second function beyond aesthetics. The result is a car that looks effortlessly clean, like a water droplet shaped by nature itself.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"//i02.appmifile.com/204_operatorx_operatorx_uploadTiptapImage/01/03/2026/b4569ac7697c5f5082f69174c8ccd330.png\"\u003eFrom the side, the cockpit silhouette takes the form of a teardrop. Every surface has been optimized for airflow, every structural member shaped with an airfoil cross-section. The body is sculpted with cutouts and airducts that embed the teardrop-shaped cockpit within a larger aerodynamic architecture, forming channels that guide air throughout the vehicle. Air enters from the front, flows through these sculpted passages, and is efficiently expelled from the rear, tracing the very path of the wind.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eXiaomi's signature design language is woven into every aspect of the concept. The cross-shaped headlights seamlessly integrate with the body while serving a functional aerodynamic purpose. At the rear, the halo-shaped taillight is more than a visual icon. It is integrated into the massive air outlet structure, where it serves as both a family design signature and a functional component of the car's aerodynamic system.\u003cimg src=\"//i02.appmifile.com/914_operatorx_operatorx_uploadTiptapImage/01/03/2026/1f90462a649ea3e21b354b8d65dadbc2.jpg\"\u003eThe rear also features the Active Wake Control System, a matrix of micro-perforations surrounding the taillight. Using real-time data on vehicle speed and angle, the system actively generates air to guide airflow, pushing turbulent air farther away from the rear of the vehicle. Unlike conventional active spoilers, this design works like an invisible hand, managing airflow while preserving the car's clean, uninterrupted surfaces.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Accretion Rims represent another breakthrough in functional design. A vortex-shaped wheel cover sits flush with the tire surface. Through its semi-transparent cover, viewers can glimpse the turbine fins inside, which actively pull air to cool the brakes during operation. The true innovation lies in the magnetic system beneath: when the car is in motion, the wheel cover remains perfectly stationary, reducing the aerodynamic drag caused by rotating wheel surfaces while creating a visually striking floating effect.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"//i02.appmifile.com/837_operatorx_operatorx_uploadTiptapImage/01/03/2026/db8252bcc70dc2f14624f6c85c837a57.jpg\"\u003eEvery aerodynamic feature on Xiaomi Vision Gran Turismo serves a purpose, some focused on reducing drag, others on generating downforce. Together, they work in perfect harmony, complementing each other with precision. Through iterative simulated testing, the concept achieves a drag coefficient of just 0.29, downforce of negative 1.2, and an aerodynamic efficiency rating of 4.1. These numbers demonstrate that Xiaomi Vision Gran Turismo is not about chasing extremes on any single metric, but about delivering peak efficiency through perfectly balanced aerodynamics, reaching new heights in the balance between low drag and high downforce for electric hypercars.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cvideo src=\"//i02.appmifile.com/15_operatorx_operatorx_uploadTiptapVideo/01/03/2026/4ae868b8f384bbef05942ee43244454b.mp4\" controls=\"true\"\u003e\u003csource src=\"//i02.appmifile.com/15_operatorx_operatorx_uploadTiptapVideo/01/03/2026/4ae868b8f384bbef05942ee43244454b.mp4\" controls=\"true\"\u003e\u003c/video\u003e\u003ch2\u003eSofa Racer: Redefining the Hypercar Interior\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe interior of a hypercar is often associated with tension and rigid seating positions. Xiaomi envisioned a different approach: an experience that is intelligent, warm, and comfortable, like racing on a sofa. This vision became the \"Sofa Racer\" concept, an interior philosophy that reimagines what a performance cockpit can be.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"//i02.appmifile.com/446_operatorx_operatorx_uploadTiptapImage/01/03/2026/ae4238fab9a1aa412006d3525881168d.jpg\" alt=\"The interior perspective showcases a modern design steering wheel and dashboard, with seats equipped with seat belts. The interior predominantly features a teal and black color scheme, and the overall design is simple yet futuristic.\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eXiaomi moves away from the traditional bucket seat logic found in most hypercars. Instead, the dashboard, door panels, and seats flow together as one cohesive loop, a continuous ring-shaped architecture that forms a cocoon-like cockpit, gently yet firmly enveloping the driver. The choice of materials reflects this warmth. Natural fabric, processed through a 3D knitting technique borrowed from the sports fashion industry, delivers a seating experience that is both breathable and supportive. It allows the driver to either focus on performance or relax, a duality of experience that defines the \"Sofa Racer\" concept.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAt the center of this space is Xiaomi Pulse, an intelligent assistant built into the dashboard. Wrapping 360 degrees around the driver, it connects to sensors throughout the vehicle, reading the environment and the driver's state, and communicating through light and sound in natural, intuitive interactions. Complementing this is Xiaomi HyperVision, a reimagined interface for Xiaomi Hyper OS that adapts dynamically to driving mode. Whether displaying minimal telemetry data on the track or immersive navigation on road trips, it always shows what matters most in the most intuitive way. Together, they transform the cockpit into a living space where information flows like conversation.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"//i02.appmifile.com/654_operatorx_operatorx_uploadTiptapImage/01/03/2026/f03972838ca48fa75effe4dec1be2a28.jpg\" alt=\"The interior perspective showcases a modern dashboard, a large steering wheel, and black seats, complemented by a bright blue and black interior design, presenting an overall futuristic feel. The dashboard displays speed and other information.\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eFocused driving remains paramount. Every physical control is crafted with the precision of a premium smartphone, buttons and stalks that deliver confidence with every press. The infinite-shaped steer-by-wire wheel puts every function within reach, blending digital information with physical controls. With hands on the wheel, the driver has total command.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2\u003eIntegrated Intelligence and the Ecosystem Vision\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eTrue to the Xiaomi family, Xiaomi Vision Gran Turismo is fully integrated into the broader \"Human x Car x Home\" smart ecosystem. Like Xiaomi SU7 and Xiaomi YU7, the concept seamlessly connects with personal devices. It senses the driver's state and adapts to their mood, not as a machine following commands, but as an intuitive companion that understands. Powered by XiaoAi AI Assistant and Xiaomi MiMo foundational model, the vehicle actively perceives and responds through light, sound, and touch, dissolving the barrier between driver and machine.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eExtending this vision beyond the vehicle, Xiaomi has conceived a driving simulator as part of the design exploration. Envisioned as an elegant piece of furniture that blends naturally into a living space, it offers a glimpse into how the Vision Gran Turismo experience could transcend the boundaries of the car itself, allowing players to practice, explore, and enjoy the art of driving from anywhere.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"//i02.appmifile.com/159_operatorx_operatorx_uploadTiptapImage/01/03/2026/5fcaf55338c1977e151d20c86f6e2d6e.png\" alt=\"A modern massage chair, designed with streamlined lines, equipped with adjustable massage devices, situated in a bright indoor environment with curtains and a sofa in the background.\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2\u003eA Historic Milestone\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eXiaomi's participation in the Vision Gran Turismo project places it among an elite group of the world's most visionary automakers. Following in the footsteps of world-renowned legacy automotive brands, Xiaomi becomes the 36th brand to join the project and creator of the 51st Vision Gran Turismo concept vehicle. As the first technology company to contribute to this legendary franchise, this recognition speaks not only to Xiaomi's automotive ambitions but to its design capabilities, technical expertise, and unique perspective as a company born in the AI and smart ecosystem era.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eXiaomi's approach represents a path distinct from the traditional fuel-vehicle era — one that integrates AI, intelligent ecosystems, and cutting-edge aerodynamics into a cohesive vision for the future of mobility.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\"The overall design maintains its simplicity while revealing an indescribably sleek and incredibly sexy curved aesthetic,\" said Kazunori Yamauchi, Producer of the\u0026nbsp;\u003cem\u003eGran Turismo\u003c/em\u003e\u0026nbsp;series. \"What impressed me most was how Xiaomi resolved the contradiction between low drag and high downforce. When I saw their complete solutions, I was truly amazed. I believe this car will become a role model for this era.\"\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eXiaomi believes technology reaches its highest purpose when it serves people and enriches experience. The Xiaomi Vision Gran Turismo expresses a new archetype for the electric hypercar — one that links human, machine, and home with continuity and care. Beyond extraordinary performance lies intelligence. Beyond speed lies comfort. Beyond the singular expression of power lies a more complete personality.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eFurther details regarding Xiaomi Vision Gran Turismo's official arrival in Gran Turismo 7 will be shared in future announcements, allowing racing enthusiasts around the world to experience it virtually and witness what happens when a technology company reimagines the hypercar.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eProduct images and videos available here: \u003ca target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://miretail.sharepoint.com/:f:/s/InternationalPRRepository/IgDFBhEcjo7ER7ltme9PCX6EAWtaBBKyQt8RtaAUfXdmZMg?e=bhEWwb\"\u003eXiaomi Vision Gran Turismo\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAbout Xiaomi Corporation\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eXiaomi Corporation was founded in April 2010 and listed on the Main Board of the Hong Kong Stock Exchange on July 9, 2018 (1810.HK). Xiaomi is a consumer electronics and smart manufacturing company with smartphones and smart hardware connected by an IoT platform at its core.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eEmbracing our vision of “Make friends with users and be the coolest company in the users’ hearts”, Xiaomi continuously pursues innovations, high-quality user experience and operational efficiency. The Company relentlessly builds amazing products with honest prices to let everyone in the world enjoy a better life through innovative technology.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eXiaomi is one of the world’s leading smartphone companies. In September 2025, the MAU reached approximately 741.7 million (including smartphones and tablets) globally. The Company has also established the world’s leading consumer AIoT (AI+IoT) platform, reached approximately 1,035.5 million smart devices connected to its platform (excluding smartphones, laptops and tablets) as of September 30, 2025. In October 2023, Xiaomi upgraded its strategy to “Human × Car × Home” smart ecosystem, seamlessly merges personal devices, smart home products, and cars. Xiaomi always centers on humanity and is committed to providing comprehensive, better connected experiences. Xiaomi products are present in more than 100 countries and regions around the world. In July 2025, Xiaomi was included in the Fortune Global 500 list for the seventh year in a row, ranking 297th.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eXiaomi is a constituent of the Hang Seng Index, Hang Seng China Enterprises Index, Hang Seng TECH Index and Hang Seng China 50 Index.\u003c/p\u003e","product_list":null,"shareCnt":"2954","material_type":"newsroom","online_time":"1774496576"},"common":null}